#. type: Title ===
#: en/data-use/modules/ROOT/pages/api-sql-downloads.adoc:135
#, no-wrap
msgid "Taxonomy columns"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/data-use/modules/ROOT/pages/api-sql-downloads.adoc:139
msgid "The `occurrence` table contains the interpreted taxonomy for each occurrence based on Catalogue of Life, as well as the verbatim taxonomy.  In addition, support for the GBIF backbone taxonomy is available through the `gbif_classification` prefixed columns, which are derived from the GBIF backbone taxonomy."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/data-use/modules/ROOT/pages/api-sql-downloads.adoc:141
msgid "The taxonomic columns populated with content from Catalogue of Life include:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: en/data-use/modules/ROOT/pages/api-sql-downloads.adoc:288
#, no-wrap
msgid "| Column | Type | Description\n\n"
"| taxonkey\n"
"| STRING\n"
"| The taxon key we have matched to for this record. This will differ from `acceptedtaxonkey` if the matched taxon is a synonym.\n\n"
"| scientificname\n"
"| STRING\n"
"| The scientific name of the taxon we have matched to for this record.\n\n"
"| acceptedtaxonkey\n"
"| STRING\n"
"| The taxon key of the accepted taxon for the match. This will be the same as `taxonkey` when the matched taxon is accepted, and will point to the accepted taxon when the match is a synonym.\n\n"
"| acceptedscientificname\n"
"| STRING\n"
"| The scientific name of the accepted taxon. This may differ from `scientificname` when the matched taxon is a synonym.\n\n"
"| genericname\n"
"| STRING\n"
"| The generic name of the matched taxon, typically the genus component of the scientific name.\n\n"
"| specificepithet\n"
"| STRING\n"
"| The specific epithet of the matched taxon, excluding the genus and any infraspecific epithet.\n\n"
"| infraspecificepithet\n"
"| STRING\n"
"| The infraspecific epithet of the matched taxon, for example the subspecies or variety epithet.\n\n"
"| taxonrank\n"
"| STRING\n"
"| The taxonomic rank of the matched taxon, for example `SPECIES`, `GENUS`, or `FAMILY`.\n\n"
"| kingdomkey\n"
"| STRING\n"
"| The taxon key for the kingdom in the classification of the matched taxon.\n\n"
"| phylumkey\n"
"| STRING\n"
"| The taxon key for the phylum in the classification of the matched taxon.\n\n"
"| classkey\n"
"| STRING\n"
"| The taxon key for the class in the classification of the matched taxon.\n\n"
"| orderkey\n"
"| STRING\n"
"| The taxon key for the order in the classification of the matched taxon.\n\n"
"| superfamilykey\n"
"| STRING\n"
"| The taxon key for the superfamily in the classification of the matched taxon.\n\n"
"| familykey\n"
"| STRING\n"
"| The taxon key for the family in the classification of the matched taxon.\n\n"
"| subfamilykey\n"
"| STRING\n"
"| The taxon key for the subfamily in the classification of the matched taxon.\n\n"
"| tribekey\n"
"| STRING\n"
"| The taxon key for the tribe in the classification of the matched taxon.\n\n"
"| subtribekey\n"
"| STRING\n"
"| The taxon key for the subtribe in the classification of the matched taxon.\n\n"
"| genuskey\n"
"| STRING\n"
"| The taxon key for the genus in the classification of the matched taxon.\n\n"
"| subgenuskey\n"
"| STRING\n"
"| The taxon key for the subgenus in the classification of the matched taxon.\n\n"
"| specieskey\n"
"| STRING\n"
"| The taxon key for the species in the classification of the matched taxon.\n\n"
"| kingdom\n"
"| STRING\n"
"| The scientific name of the kingdom in the classification of the matched taxon.\n\n"
"| phylum\n"
"| STRING\n"
"| The scientific name of the phylum in the classification of the matched taxon.\n\n"
"| class\n"
"| STRING\n"
"| The scientific name of the class in the classification of the matched taxon.\n\n"
"| order\n"
"| STRING\n"
"| The scientific name of the order in the classification of the matched taxon.\n\n"
"| superfamily\n"
"| STRING\n"
"| The scientific name of the superfamily in the classification of the matched taxon.\n\n"
"| family\n"
"| STRING\n"
"| The scientific name of the family in the classification of the matched taxon.\n\n"
"| subfamily\n"
"| STRING\n"
"| The scientific name of the subfamily in the classification of the matched taxon.\n\n"
"| tribe\n"
"| STRING\n"
"| The scientific name of the tribe in the classification of the matched taxon.\n\n"
"| subtribe\n"
"| STRING\n"
"| The scientific name of the subtribe in the classification of the matched taxon.\n\n"
"| genus\n"
"| STRING\n"
"| The scientific name of the genus in the classification of the matched taxon.\n\n"
"| subgenus\n"
"| STRING\n"
"| The scientific name of the subgenus in the classification of the matched taxon.\n\n"
"| species\n"
"| STRING\n"
"| The scientific name of the species in the classification of the matched taxon.\n\n"
"| iucnredlistcategory\n"
"| STRING\n"
"| The IUCN Red List category associated with the matched taxon, when available.\n\n"
"| taxonkeys\n"
"| ARRAY<STRING>\n"
"| All taxon keys for the entire classification of the matched taxon, from kingdom to species. This includes the `taxonkey` for the matched taxon, and the `acceptedtaxonkey` for the accepted taxon. It also includes non-linnean ranks such as subfamily, tribe, and subtribe.\n\n"
"| taxonomicissue\n"
"| ARRAY<STRING>\n"
"| Taxonomic issues identified while matching or resolving the taxon.\n\n"
"| taxonomicstatus\n"
"| STRING\n"
"| The taxonomic status of the matched taxon, for example `ACCEPTED`, `SYNONYM`\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/data-use/modules/ROOT/pages/api-sql-downloads.adoc:292
msgid "All of these fields are also available for the GBIF Backbone using the `occurrence.gbif_classification` prefix in SELECT and WHERE clauses."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: en/data-use/modules/ROOT/pages/api-sql-downloads.adoc:305
#, no-wrap
msgid "SELECT\n"
"  occurrence.gbif_classification.phylum,\n"
"  occurrence.gbif_classification.class,\n"
"  occurrence.gbif_classification.\"order\",\n"
"  occurrence.gbif_classification.family,\n"
"  occurrence.gbif_classification.genus,\n"
"  occurrence.gbif_classification.species,\n"
"  occurrence.gbif_classification.taxonrank\n"
"FROM occurrence\n"
"WHERE occurrence.gbif_classification.kingdom = 'Animalia'\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Block title
#: en/data-use/modules/ROOT/pages/api-sql-downloads.adoc:309
#, no-wrap
msgid "Quoting column names"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block =
#: en/data-use/modules/ROOT/pages/api-sql-downloads.adoc:312
msgid "The SQL parser is strict, and column names that are also SQL keywords must be quoted. This affects the columns `\"year\"`, `\"month\"`, `\"day\"`, `\"order\"`, `\"group\"`, `\"language\"`, `\"references\"` and `\"member\"`.  They must be quoted even if qualified with the table name as in `occurrence.\"year\"` or `\"occurrence\".\"year\"`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/data-use/modules/ROOT/pages/api-sql-downloads.adoc:315
#, no-wrap
msgid "Query validation"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/data-use/modules/ROOT/pages/api-sql-downloads.adoc:318
msgid "You can validate your queries using the validation API call."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: en/data-use/modules/ROOT/pages/api-sql-downloads.adoc:322
#, no-wrap
msgid "curl --include --header \"Content-Type: application/json\" --data @query.json https://api.gbif.org/v1/occurrence/download/request/validate\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/data-use/modules/ROOT/pages/api-sql-downloads.adoc:325
msgid "Your query will be returned if it is valid, and an error message with an explanation will be returned if it is invalid."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/data-use/modules/ROOT/pages/api-sql-downloads.adoc:327
#, no-wrap
msgid "Troubleshooting"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/data-use/modules/ROOT/pages/api-sql-downloads.adoc:330
msgid "Many GBIF APIs are tolerant of small differences in how they are queried — you can make an occurrence download query using the search parameter `taxonKey`, `taxon_key`, `TAXONKEY` and so on, and using the value `1`, `'1'`, `\"1\"`, `{nbsp}1`, `\"{nbsp}01\"` etc."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/data-use/modules/ROOT/pages/api-sql-downloads.adoc:332
msgid "The SQL API is less forgiving, so some common parts of queries must be specified exactly as documented."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/data-use/modules/ROOT/pages/api-sql-downloads.adoc:334
msgid "Within the SQL query itself:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/data-use/modules/ROOT/pages/api-sql-downloads.adoc:336
msgid "If column names are quoted they must use double quotes and lowercase: `\"year\"`, `\"basisofrecord\"`.  It's only necessary to quote column names that are also SQL functions: `\"year\"`, `\"month\"`, `\"day\"`, `\"order\"`, `\"group\"`, `\"language\"`, `\"references\"` and `\"member\"`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/data-use/modules/ROOT/pages/api-sql-downloads.adoc:337
msgid "When column and function names aren't quoted, the letter case doesn't matter: `basisOfRecord`, `basisofrecord`, `gbif_eeargcode(…)`, `GBIF_EEARGCode(…)`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/data-use/modules/ROOT/pages/api-sql-downloads.adoc:338
msgid "String values use single quotes, like `basisOfRecord = 'HUMAN_OBSERVATION'`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/data-use/modules/ROOT/pages/api-sql-downloads.adoc:339
msgid "SQL comments (lines beginning `--{nbsp}`) cannot be included in queries."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/data-use/modules/ROOT/pages/api-sql-downloads.adoc:340
msgid "Columns with numeric types must be filtered using numbers, not quoted string values — use `\"year\" IN (2020, 2021)` or `startdayofyear >= 200`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/data-use/modules/ROOT/pages/api-sql-downloads.adoc:341
msgid "Array values (including vocabulary lineages) should be converted to delimited strings, for example `CONCAT_WS(' | ', recordedByID)` and `CONCAT_WS(' | ', occurrence.lifestage.lineage)`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/data-use/modules/ROOT/pages/api-sql-downloads.adoc:343
msgid "When converting the SQL query to JSON for submission to the API:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/data-use/modules/ROOT/pages/api-sql-downloads.adoc:345
msgid "JSON uses double quotes for attributes and values, so when the SQL is written values containing double quotes must have these escaped using `\\\"`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/data-use/modules/ROOT/pages/api-sql-downloads.adoc:346
msgid "Newlines, if used, should be replaced with either spaces ` ` or `\\n`"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: en/data-use/modules/ROOT/pages/api-sql-downloads.adoc:357
#, no-wrap
msgid "{\n"
"  \"sendNotification\": true,\n"
"  \"notificationAddresses\": [\n"
"    \"userEmail@example.org\"\n"
"  ],\n"
"  \"format\": \"SQL_TSV_ZIP\",\n"
"  \"sql\": \"SELECT DISTINCT \\\"year\\\" \\n FROM occurrence \\n WHERE \\\"year\\\" > 2000\";\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/data-use/modules/ROOT/pages/api-sql-downloads.adoc:360
msgid "It can be convenient to work with neatly formatted SQL files, and convert them to JSON format automatically:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: en/data-use/modules/ROOT/pages/api-sql-downloads.adoc:365
#, no-wrap
msgid "# Using jq\n"
"grep -v -- '--' neat-query.sql | jq -R -s .\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: en/data-use/modules/ROOT/pages/api-sql-downloads.adoc:368
#, no-wrap
msgid "# Using Python\n"
"grep -v -- '--' neat-query.sql | python3 -c 'import sys, json; print(json.dumps(sys.stdin.read()))'\n"
msgstr ""

